{"step_index":396,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T16:18:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-20T12:18:38-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-20T12:18:38-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/aiSmsService.ts`\nTotal Lines: 116\nTotal Bytes: 5372\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import { Lead, CallLog, AppSettings } from '../types';\n2: import { SettingsRepository } from '../db/settingsRepository';\n3: import { CallLogsRepository } from '../db/callLogsRepository';\n4: \n5: export class AiSmsService {\n6:   /**\n7:    * Generates a subtly persuasive, warm, and tailored SMS message for Florida educators\n8:    * based on their FRS Report Card, previous call logs, and meeting preferences.\n9:    */\n10:   static async generatePersuasiveSMS(\n11:     lead: Lead,\n12:     currentDisposition?: string,\n13:     providedApiKey?: string,\n14:     toneFocus?: 'meeting_confirmation' | 'unanswered_followup' | 'drop_bonus_focus' | 'planning_period'\n15:   ): Promise<string> {\n16:     let key = providedApiKey;\n17:     if (!key || key.trim().length === 0) {\n18:       const settings = await SettingsRepository.getSettings();\n19:       key = settings.gemini_api_key;\n20:     }\n21: \n22:     // If no API key, return a high-converting default ValuTeachers template\n23:     if (!key || key.trim().length === 0) {\n24:       return this.getFallbackSMS(lead);\n25:     }\n26: \n27:     try {\n28:       const history = await CallLogsRepository.getLogsForLead(lead.id);\n29:       const settings = await SettingsRepository.getSettings();\n30:       const agentName = settings.user_name || 'Alex';\n31: \n32:       const historySummary = history\n33:         .slice(0, 4)\n34:         .map(\n35:           (h) =>\n36:             `- Attempt at ${new Date(h.timestamp).toLocaleDateString()}: Disposition \"${h.disposition}\"${\n37:               h.note ? `, Note: \"${h.note}\"` : ''\n38:             }`\n39:         )\n40:         .join('\\n');\n41: \n42:       const preferredTimes = (lead.meeting_preferences || []).join(', ') || 'planning period';\n43:       const interests = (lead.frs_interests || []).join(', ') || 'Florida State Retirement & 403(b) options';\n44: \n45:       const prompt = `\n46: You are an expert sales copywriter specialized in educational finance and retirement planning for Florida public school teachers (Florida Retirement System / FRS) working on behalf of ValuTeachers.\n47: \n48: Context for Educator:\n49: - Educator Name: ${lead.name}\n50: - School / District: ${lead.school || 'Florida School District'}\n51: - Planning Period / Room: ${lead.planning_period || 'N/A'}, Room ${lead.room_number || 'N/A'}\n52: - Years in FRS: ${lead.years_in_frs || 'N/A'} years\n53: - FRS Knowledge Level: \"${lead.frs_knowledge || 'Moderate'}\"\n54: - Specific Needs / Inquiries Checked on Report Card: ${interests}\n55: - Educator's Written Question: \"${lead.custom_questions || 'None'}\"\n56: - Requested Meeting Availability: ${preferredTimes}\n57: - Current Call Outcome: ${currentDisposition || 'Follow-up'}\n58: - Previous Contact History & Notes:\n59: ${historySummary || 'First outreach attempt.'}\n60: - ValuTeachers Representative Name: ${agentName}\n61: \n62: Tone & Strategy Guidelines:\n63: 1. Extremely, yet SUBTLY persuasive, empathetic, highly professional, and respectful of a busy teacher's schedule.\n64: 2. Sound like a dedicated local educator advocate, NEVER like a spammy or aggressive salesperson.\n65: 3. Reference their school (${lead.school || 'your school'}) or their specific inquiry (e.g. 5% bonus, DROP options, or 403b clarity) naturally so they recognize their own submission.\n66: 4. If they requested specific meeting times (${preferredTimes}), reference it directly so it feels like a seamless confirmation.\n67: 5. Keep it concise (under 200-240 characters) so it reads effortlessly on mobile lock screens.\n68: 6. Provide a frictionless low-pressure call to action (e.g. \"Does [time] still work for a quick 5-min review, or is tomorrow better?\").\n69: 7. Output ONLY the raw SMS text message. Do not wrap in quotes or add conversational preamble.\n70: `;\n71: \n72:       const endpoint = `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-2.5-flash:generateContent?key=${key}`;\n73: \n74:       const response = await fetch(endpoint, {\n75:         method: 'POST',\n76:         headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n77:         body: JSON.stringify({\n78:           contents: [{ parts: [{ text: prompt }] }],\n79:           generationConfig: {\n80:             temperature: 0.3,\n81:             maxOutputTokens: 180,\n82:           },\n83:         }),\n84:       });\n85: \n86:       if (!response.ok) {\n87:         throw new Error(`Gemini API returned status ${response.status}`);\n88:       }\n89: \n90:       const data = await response.json();\n91:       const text = data?.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.text?.trim();\n92:       if (text) {\n93:         return text.replace(/^[\"']|[\"']$/g, '');\n94:       }\n95:     } catch (e) {\n96:       console.warn('AI SMS generation failed, falling back to local copy:', e);\n97:     }\n98: \n99:     return this.getFallbackSMS(lead);\n100:   }\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":397,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T16:18:38Z","thinking":"**Focusing on Scheduling**\n\nI'm now writing the upgraded `aiSmsService.ts` file, with the sole focus on scheduling the planning period sit-down. My prompt and fallback methods are being updated.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import { Lead, CallLog, AppSettings } from '../types';\nimport { SettingsRepository } from '../db/settingsRepository';\nimport { CallLogsRepository } from '../db/callLogsRepository';\n\nexport class AiSmsService {\n  /**\n   * Generates a subtly persuasive, warm, and tailored SMS message for Florida educators\n   * where the primary objective is scheduling a quick in-person sit-down during their\n   * requested planning period or preferred time window.\n   */\n  static async generatePersuasiveSMS(\n    lead: Lead,\n    currentDisposition?: string,\n    providedApiKey?: string,\n    toneFocus?: 'meeting_confirmation' | 'unanswered_followup' | 'drop_bonus_focus' | 'planning_period'\n  ): Promise<string> {\n    let key = providedApiKey;\n    if (!key || key.trim().length === 0) {\n      const settings = await SettingsRepository.getSettings();\n      key = settings.gemini_api_key;\n    }\n\n    // If no API key, return a high-converting default ValuTeachers sit-down template\n    if (!key || key.trim().length === 0) {\n      return this.getFallbackSMS(lead);\n    }\n\n    try {\n      const history = await CallLogsRepository.getLogsForLead(lead.id);\n      const settings = await SettingsRepository.getSettings();\n      const agentName = settings.user_name || 'Alex';\n\n      const historySummary = history\n        .slice(0, 4)\n        .map(\n          (h) =>\n            `- Attempt at ${new Date(h.timestamp).toLocaleDateString()}: Disposition \"${h.disposition}\"${\n              h.note ? `, Note: \"${h.note}\"` : ''\n            }`\n        )\n        .join('\\n');\n\n      const preferredTimes = (lead.meeting_preferences || []).join(', ') || 'your planning period';\n      const interests = (lead.frs_interests || []).join(', ') || 'Florida State Retirement & 403(b) options';\n\n      const prompt = `\nYou are an expert consultative copywriter for ValuTeachers working with Florida public school teachers (Florida Retirement System / FRS).\n\nPRIMARY OBJECTIVE:\nSchedule a brief, convenient in-person sit-down with the teacher (at their school during their planning period or in their classroom/room number as indicated on their report card) to review their FRS state pension calculation, 403(b) options, DROP timeline, and the 5% bonus.\n\nContext for Educator:\n- Educator Name: ${lead.name}\n- School / District: ${lead.school || 'Florida School District'}\n- Planning Period / Room: ${lead.planning_period || 'N/A'}${lead.room_number ? `, Room ${lead.room_number}` : ''}\n- Years in FRS: ${lead.years_in_frs || 'N/A'} years\n- FRS Knowledge Level: \"${lead.frs_knowledge || 'Moderate'}\"\n- Specific Needs / Inquiries Checked on Report Card: ${interests}\n- Educator's Written Question: \"${lead.custom_questions || 'None'}\"\n- Requested Sit-Down / Meeting Availability: ${preferredTimes}\n- Current Call Outcome: ${currentDisposition || 'Follow-up'}\n- Previous Contact History & Notes:\n${historySummary || 'First outreach attempt.'}\n- ValuTeachers Representative Name: ${agentName}\n\nStrategy & Tone Guidelines:\n1. Focus on scheduling the SIT-DOWN: Frame the message around locking in a quick 10-15 minute sit-down during their planning period (${lead.planning_period || 'planning period'}) or preferred slot (${preferredTimes}).\n2. Mention being on campus / visiting ${lead.school || 'the school'} to make the sit-down feel effortless, low-friction, and convenient.\n3. Subtly persuasive & consultative: Avoid aggressive sales language. Speak as a trusted educational retirement advisor who received their handwritten request.\n4. Seamlessly incorporate their specific interest (e.g. 5% bonus on contributions, DROP calculation, or 403b clarity).\n5. Length: Keep between 180 and 240 characters for immediate readability on mobile screens.\n6. Frictionless Call-to-Action: Ask a simple confirmation question (e.g. \"I'll be at ${lead.school || 'the school'} this week—would ${preferredTimes} work for a quick sit-down in your room, or is tomorrow better?\").\n7. Output ONLY the raw SMS text without quotes or preamble.\n`;\n\n      const endpoint = `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-2.5-flash:generateContent?key=${key}`;\n\n      const response = await fetch(endpoint, {\n        method: 'POST',\n        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify({\n          contents: [{ parts: [{ text: prompt }] }],\n          generationConfig: {\n            temperature: 0.3,\n            maxOutputTokens: 180,\n          },\n        }),\n      });\n\n      if (!response.ok) {\n        throw new Error(`Gemini API returned status ${response.status}`);\n      }\n\n      const data = await response.json();\n      const text = data?.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.text?.trim();\n      if (text) {\n        return text.replace(/^[\"']|[\"']$/g, '');\n      }\n    } catch (e) {\n      console.warn('AI SMS generation failed, falling back to local copy:', e);\n    }\n\n    return this.getFallbackSMS(lead);\n  }\n\n  private static getFallbackSMS(lead: Lead): string {\n    const firstName = lead.name ? lead.name.split(' ')[0] : 'there';\n    const school = lead.school || 'your school';\n    const planning = lead.planning_period || 'your planning period';\n    const room = lead.room_number ? ` in Room ${lead.room_number}` : '';\n    const primaryTime =\n      lead.meeting_preferences && lead.meeting_preferences.length > 0\n        ? lead.meeting_preferences[0].replace(/^[0-9]\\.\\s*/, '')\n        : `during ${planning}`;\n\n    if (lead.years_in_frs && parseInt(lead.years_in_frs, 10) >= 15) {\n      return `Hi ${firstName}, this is Alex with ValuTeachers. I have your FRS Report Card from ${school} regarding your ${lead.years_in_frs} yrs of service and DROP options. I'll be at the school this week—does ${primaryTime} work for a quick 10-min sit-down${room}?`;\n    }\n\n    return `Hi ${firstName}, this is Alex with ValuTeachers. I received your FRS Report Card from ${school} regarding your retirement & 403(b) review. I'll be visiting campus this week—does ${primaryTime} work for a quick 10-min sit-down during ${planning}?`;\n  }\n}\n","Description":"Enhanced AiSmsService with primary focus on scheduling on-campus planning period sit-downs","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\services\\aiSmsService.ts","toolAction":"Updating AiSmsService for sit-down scheduling","toolSummary":"Update AiSmsService.ts sit-down focus"}}]}
